<article class="env-lemma" id="047K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/047K">Lemma <span data-tag="047K">39.7.1</span>.</a> If $(G, m)$ is a group scheme over a field $k$, then the multiplication map $m : G \times _ k G \to G$ is open. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The multiplication map is isomorphic to the projection map $\text{pr}_0 : G \times _ k G \to G$ because the diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ G \times _ k G \ar[d]^ m \ar[rrr]_{(g, g') \mapsto (m(g, g'), g')} &  &  &  G \times _ k G \ar[d]^{(g, g') \mapsto g} \\  G \ar[rrr]^{\text{id}} &  &  &  G }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is commutative with isomorphisms as horizontal arrows. The projection is open by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0383" data-tag="0383">29.24.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>